&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VML is a global creative company that combines brand experience, customer experience, and commerce to create connected brands&amp;nbsp;that drive growth. Guided by a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Human First&lt;/strong&gt; philosophy, VML is known for its innovative work for brands and consistently ranks among the world’s leading creative companies, including the WARC Creative 100.&amp;nbsp;VML’s global network spans 55+ markets with principal offices in Buenos Aires, Kansas City, London, New York, São Paulo, Shanghai and Singapore.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VML is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.vml.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d4b7d1c3-8ad6-4b6d-ab45-d3cb5a3aebe1&quot;&gt;www.vml.com &lt;/a&gt;and follow along on  &lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__urldefense.com_v3_-5F-5Fhttps-3A_www.linkedin.com_company_vml_-5F-5F-3B-21-21JboVxjCXSME-21OhlpCfbkl1UcWPwns1-2DGtvHOzFh0QwHV49fsPgGw-2DVCCU1bCg8aQFI9vN-2Dy-2DVwaQcITH2j2XKzGKBIFRLYf2AUWVYY1dFGK6-24&amp;amp;d=DwMFaQ&amp;amp;c=euGZstcaTDllvimEN8b7jXrwqOf-v5A_CdpgnVfiiMM&amp;amp;r=zouFnm4jZMgDFaYF1uVcRY3rbgHWPca_luUrBUkT6Yc&amp;amp;m=QzcCgXCAOjzj5hiU48_CKOdHRSJ4_YpuqfviT9yjlzH5VrkzySTZ-WaQXlYAnj4W&amp;amp;s=jJ7q5V70u9oUx7ONPm5jC3IK8y6vxDilX6BGTlqlWlA&amp;amp;e=&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;a3ef68bf-16fb-4ebc-9ca9-406007d6cefc&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;#WeAreVML.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Programme Lead / Operations Director&lt;/strong&gt; on a 3 month FTC to spearhead a major operational stabilisation and governance programme across one of our flagship global accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will lead a critical programme to standardise operating models, establish robust commercial and delivery controls, and ensure full operational audit-readiness across creative, media, CX, and technology workstreams. You will bridge senior strategy with hands-on delivery—moving a complex, multi-market operation toward clear, verifiable governance and sustainable ways of working.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct the overarching governance and stabilisation programme; own the master roadmap, milestone tracking, and executive governance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational &amp;amp; Commercial Controls:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with workstream leads across Finance, Operations, Tech, and Commercial to design and embed gate registers, approval frameworks, and compliance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Stakeholder Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive active adoption of standard processes across service towers, regional delivery hubs, and senior client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Tooling Optimisation:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive workflow tool standardisation (including enterprise workflow systems such as Workfront), establishing automated tracking and reporting against contractual SLAs and performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Readiness &amp;amp; Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead readiness preparations for upcoming corporate and operational audit reviews, coordinating evidence gathering, walk-throughs, and response tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Future Operating Model Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate programme outcomes and proven controls into standard operating procedures (SOPs), role definitions, and a seamless handover to Business-As-Usual (BAU) operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior &amp;amp; Hands-On:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience steering complex programmes with executive stakeholders, paired with the appetite to roll up your sleeves and drive day-to-day execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influential Leader:&lt;/strong&gt; Adept at aligning cross-functional teams—including Delivery, Finance, Tech, Legal, and senior client partners—who do not report to you directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Disciplinary Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Comfortable translating between delivery operations, commercial agreements, technology workflows, and contractual governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years within a top-tier agency, management consultancy, or corporate marketing operations environment, leading large-scale operating model transformations, compliance programmes, or audit-readiness initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Governance Acumen:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid background in performance- and output-based commercial frameworks, enterprise SLA management, and workflow tools. Familiarity with AI-enabled productivity tools is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear &amp;amp; Decisive Communicator:&lt;/strong&gt; Calm under tight timelines, structured in problem-solving, and crisp in executive-level documentation and presenting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office an average of four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;WPP (VML) is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;scxw176048299&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click &quot;Submit Application&quot;, this will send any information you add below to VML. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;. California residents should read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is experiencing tremendous growth as enterprise organizations transition from evaluating AI to rapidly deploying production-grade AI systems. This role exists to redefine how we enable our largest customers to move faster, activate their data workforces, and convert platform investments into measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Manager of Capability Engineering &amp;amp; AI Adoption for EMEA, you will lead two complementary teams: a regional group of Customer Enablement Architects who act as trusted advisors and builder-enablement partners for Databricks’ largest, most complex accounts, and the EMEA Scaled User Programmes team, whose mission is to design and execute broad, high-impact enablement initiatives across the region. Operating at the intersection of technical depth, program strategy, and business outcomes, you will translate advanced product roadmaps into both personalized, just-in-time capability programs and scalable enablement engines that meet customers wherever they are in their modernization and AI adoption journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, coach, and develop an elite regional team of Customer Enablement Architects across EMEA, setting a high standard for technical depth, customer impact, and creative problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capability Engineering at Scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Redesign enterprise enablement workflows, moving away from legacy episodic models to continuous, contextual, and hyper-personalized capability building aligned with customers&#39; modernization curves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Adoption &amp;amp; MAU Activation:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner directly with account teams and field leadership to diagnose capability blockers and drive measurable increases in Monthly Active Users (MAU) across strategic enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Builder Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Cultivate a builder culture within the team to design and deploy custom enablement applications, tools, and prototypes (e.g., via Databricks Apps, Genie, or agentic frameworks) when standard curricula fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Stakeholder Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct deep discovery sessions with enterprise technical leaders and C-suite executives, aligning strategic capability roadmaps with the customer&#39;s high-level AI transformation goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Operational Integrity:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the regional voice into global curriculum and certification teams to prioritize EMEA market needs and skill gaps, while maintaining strict operational rigor with training logistics teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Regional Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Undertake regional travel across EMEA to engage directly with strategic enterprise accounts on-site , lead high-stakes executive alignment sessions , and provide hands-on leadership to a geographically dispersed team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep foundational understanding of lakehouse architecture, data engineering/ETL pipelines, data governance, and generative AI/agentic workflows to earn immediate respect from customer data teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Builder Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; A non-negotiable track record of personally designing, building, and deploying working prototypes, automation tools, or technical apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer-Facing Solutioning:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior experience in a solutions architect, customer success engineering, customer enablement, or advanced delivery role, with a proven ability to confidently navigate ambiguity and discover core user friction points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement Reinvention:&lt;/strong&gt; Passion for moving beyond legacy classroom-style or completion-centric learning models into just-in-time, contextual capability building embedded directly in user workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Business Insight:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to connect technical skill outcomes to core P&amp;amp;L levers, influence renewals/expansions, and collaborate effectively with sales on strategic account planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA Fluency &amp;amp; Mobility (Required)&lt;/strong&gt;: Lived experience operating across EMEA markets . Ability and willingness to travel to meet customers and support team members across different EMEA locations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership and Credibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior experience leading and managing technical or customer-facing engineering teams, with a proven ability to mentor talent, hold a high bar, and build a cohesive team identity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
